  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Turn on the rebound",
  "description": "Pairs with one ball, in front of a wall, a fence, a board or a bench lying on its side. The cones in the diagram show the wall. The pair stands about 10–15 metres from the wall and one of them has the ball.\n\nThe first player dribbles towards the wall and passes against it from a few metres away. On the rebound they take the ball into a turn – for example with the inside, the outside or the sole – dribble back to their partner and hand the ball over. Then it is the partner's turn. Try a new turn each time.\n\nVariants: the partner copies the turn you just did. Do a feint before the turn and speed up straight after it. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass firmly enough that you can take the rebound with you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Move towards the ball and turn with your first touch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Bend your knees and get low in the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Come out of the turn at full speed with the ball close."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
